peror Shenzong of Song (25 May 1048 – 1 April 1085), personal name Zhao Xu, was the sixth emperor of the Song dynasty of China. His original personal name was Zhao Zhongzhen but he changed it to \"Zhao Xu\" after he acceded to the throne. He reigned from 1067 until his death in 1085 and is best known for supporting Wang Anshi's New Policies. He was a particularly active monarch concerned with expanding Song territory and solving its fiscal, bureaucratic, and military problems through major reforms, but his reign remains controversial due to military failures and the varied effects of his changes.","wp_description":"Emperor of China from 1067 to 1085","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emperor_Shenzong_of_Song","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/84/Shenzong.jpg","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Shenzong.jpg/960px-Shenzong.jpg","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1067,"display_to":1085}